---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import "../../styles/guide.css";

// The webhook URL of the API this site documents. Origin only, the route carries its own /api/v1
const apiBaseURL = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL || "http://localhost:8080";
const webhookURL = `${apiBaseURL}/api/v1/webhooks/jellyfin`;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const destination = `Webhook Name:       biinge
Webhook Url:        ${webhookURL}
Notification Type:  User Data Saved
User Filter:        <your Jellyfin user>
Item Type:          Movies, Episodes
Send All Properties: on`;

const header = `Key:    Authorization
Value:  Bearer <the token from the app>`;

const rules = [
  { event: "A movie you want to watch or are watching", result: "Moves to watched" },
  { event: "An episode of a show you want to watch or are watching", result: "Marks the episode. The show becomes watching, or watched once every season is done" },
  { event: "A movie or an episode you have already watched", result: "Nothing changes" },
  { event: "An episode of a show you have already watched", result: "Nothing changes" },
  { event: "A title that is not in your library", result: "Nothing changes" },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Jellyfin sync - biinge"
  description="Let Jellyfin mark movies and episodes watched in biinge the moment you finish them."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="page">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-head">
        <p class="eyebrow-label">Integrations</p>
        <h1>Sync watched marks from Jellyfin.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Finish a movie or an episode in Jellyfin and biinge marks it watched.
          Sync runs one way, from Jellyfin to biinge. It only touches titles that are already in your library.
          Setup takes a token from the app and one webhook destination on the Jellyfin server.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prereq">
        <h2>Before you start</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Jellyfin 12</strong> with the Webhook plugin from the Jellyfin plugin catalog</li>
          <li><strong>Admin rights</strong> on that Jellyfin server. Only an admin can add a webhook destination</li>
          <li>
            Movies and episodes scraped by Jellyfin's built-in TMDB providers. That is where the ids come from.
            A library scraped only from local NFO files may lack them
          </li>
          <li>A biinge server the Jellyfin server can reach over HTTPS</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <ol class="steps">
        <li class="step">
          <div class="step-head"><span class="num">1</span><h3>Generate a token in the app</h3></div>
          <p>
            Open <strong>Profile</strong>, then <strong>Jellyfin</strong>, and tap <strong>Generate token</strong>.
            The app shows the token once, with a copy button. Copy it now. It is not shown again.
          </p>
          <p class="note">
            This is a Jellyfin token, not the app's access or refresh token. It can add watched marks to your library,
            so treat it as a password. Generate a new one to replace it, or revoke it from the same screen.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li class="step">
          <div class="step-head"><span class="num">2</span><h3>Add a webhook destination in Jellyfin</h3></div>
          <p>
            In the Jellyfin dashboard open <strong>Plugins</strong>, then <strong>Webhook</strong>, and add a
            <strong>Generic Destination</strong> with these values.
          </p>
          <CodeBlock code={destination} label="destination" />
          <p class="note">
            Set the <strong>User Filter</strong> to your own Jellyfin user. Every event that carries the token lands on
            the biinge account that owns it. Without the filter, plays by other people on the server would too.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li class="step">
          <div class="step-head"><span class="num">3</span><h3>Add the request header</h3></div>
          <p>
            In the same destination, add one <strong>Request Header</strong>. Paste the token from step 1 after
            <code>Bearer</code>, with a single space between them.
          </p>
          <CodeBlock code={header} label="header" />
          <p class="note">
            The token is the only thing biinge checks. Anyone who has it can add watched marks to your library until
            you revoke it.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li class="step">
          <div class="step-head"><span class="num">4</span><h3>Watch something</h3></div>
          <p>
            Save the destination, then finish a movie or an episode in Jellyfin. Marking it played from the Jellyfin
            UI works too. The mark shows up in biinge on the next refresh.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="config">
        <h2>What a play does</h2>
        <p class="config-lead">
          Jellyfin only adds marks. It never removes one, never adds a title, and never changes a watched title to
          anything else. Unmarking stays in the app.
        </p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>You finish</th><th>In biinge</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {rules.map((row) => (
                <tr>
                  <td>{row.event}</td>
                  <td>{row.result}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="config">
        <h2>When a mark does not show up</h2>
        <ul class="prod-list">
          <li>
            Check the Webhook plugin log on the Jellyfin server. It records every delivery and the status the API
            answered with
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>401</code> means the token is missing, wrong or revoked. Generate a new one and update the header
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>422</code> means biinge could not resolve the title. The movie has no TMDB id, the episode has no
            TVDB or IMDb id, or TMDB does not know that id. Refresh the item's metadata in Jellyfin
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>502</code> means TMDB did not answer. The plugin does not retry, so mark the title in the app
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>503</code> means biinge's database was unreachable. The plugin does not retry, so mark the title in
            the app
          </li>
          <li>
            A movie or a show that is not in your library is ignored on purpose. Add it in the app first
          </li>
          <li>
            Every accepted event is kept on the server with what biinge did about it. The
            <a href={`${base}docs/api/#jellyfin-webhook`}>API reference</a> lists the fields the endpoint reads
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
